From 3faa1ccbc461187ce5f21d29a162d0b7d1e1d17b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: dinadur <59811564+dinadur@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 18:43:55 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 09/18] B70: product comparisons by 'comparing' + one repair
 fetch before withholding

extract_targets only recognised 'compare X, Y and Z for/on' and 'research X
for', and used only the first matching clause. 'Research the best X under $N
for Y, comparing A, B and C' therefore yielded no alternatives, so named
three-product comparisons took the single-candidate path (and its
candidate_budget_missing rule). Add the 'comparing' clause and use the first
clause that names 2-8 alternatives.

With HERMES_PRODUCT_RESEARCH_REPAIR_FETCH=1, an unready receipt request after
the 4-search / 2-extract budget is spent no longer withholds at once: the
controller grants exactly one more web_search and web_extract for the turn
and names the missing evidence. A second unready receipt request withholds as
before.

Replay of the seven product turns withheld on 2026-10-07 against the receipt
viability gate: the parser fix alone makes 1 ready; the rest lacked two
independent source families with the budget already spent, which the repair
fetch addresses.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
